-Every mapping declared on the shared handler is merged into every variant of `WorkItem`, so a member that only
-the shared handler populates, like `Title` here, is populated on whichever variant the entity is in. The
-`CHR0024` analyzer counts the entering events and the shared handlers of a variant's group as mapping sources. Like any other
-non-entering event, a shared mapping can only update an already-active variant — it can never create or
-resurrect one, so it is safe to share across a group whose members enter at different times.
