+This example combines entry, build-status updates, and a shared title mapping. Follow one entity key through the events: issue creation puts it in the backlog, pull request creation moves it out, and later build or title changes update only the active variant.
+
 <ChronicleClientTabs snippet="projections/model-bound/variants/full-example" />
 
 ## Best practices
 
-1. **Pick an identity type that means something on its own** — `WorkItem` in the examples above, not a
-   marker interface with no purpose beyond grouping. It is the type every variant, and every shared
-   handler, points back to.
-2. **Give every variant the properties that stage of the entity needs.** A shared property
-   that every stage needs belongs on a `[GlobalFor<T>]` handler instead of being copy-pasted onto each
-   variant.
-3. **Variants suit both kinds of shape.** Use them when the stages genuinely diverge, each with properties
-   the others do not have. Use them just as well when the stages share nearly the same shape: each
-   variant is its own collection, so a query for one stage reads only that stage, with no `Status`
-   property to filter on or index. The two uses are not mutually exclusive.
-4. **Remember each variant is its own collection.** There is no built-in query that spans a whole group —
-   a caller that needs "this entity, whichever stage it's currently in" queries each variant explicitly
-   (or by its shared key) rather than assuming a single combined collection.
+Choose an identity type that names the entity, such as the work item in these examples, and give each variant the properties its callers need. Keep common event mappings on a shared handler when they apply to every stage.
+
+Plan queries around the separate collections. There is no built-in query spanning a variant group: a caller that needs an entity regardless of stage must query the variants explicitly, using the shared entity key where appropriate. For reading a particular variant by key, continue with [Read-model consistency](../../read-models/consistency.md).
